-- title:
--   Bound on dim H¹ for a group with cyclic quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $G$ a finite group, and let $A$ be a representation of $G$ over $k$ with $A$ finite-dimensional over $k$, the action being written $\rho$. Let $S$ be a normal subgroup of $G$ with $G/S$ finite, let $t \in S$ be such that $S$ is contained in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $t$ (so $S$ is the cyclic group $\langle t\rangle$), and let $\varphi \in G$ be an element whose class in $G/S$ generates $G/S$, in the sense that every element of $G/S$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\varphi S$. Let $m$ be a natural number with $\varphi^{-1} t \varphi = t^{m}$, and assume moreover $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in \langle t \rangle$. The latter hypothesis guarantees that $\rho(\varphi)$ carries the image of $\rho(t) - 1$ into itself, hence induces an endomorphism `frobeniusOnCoinvariants` of the quotient $A_t = A/\mathrm{im}(\rho(t)-1)$. The conclusion is the inequality
--   $$\dim_k H^1(G, A) \le \dim_k A^{G} + \dim_k \ker\bigl(m\cdot \overline{\rho(\varphi)} - 1 : A_t \to A_t\bigr),$$
--   where $A^{G}$ denotes the invariants of $\rho$ and the first summand of the endomorphism is the $m$-fold sum of the induced map on coinvariants.
--
--   This is the upper-bound half of the local Euler-characteristic inequality at a prime $\ell$ different from the residue characteristic, formulated for a finite group of tame shape: cyclic inertia $\langle t\rangle$ with cyclic quotient generated by a Frobenius lift $\varphi$ satisfying $\varphi^{-1}t\varphi = t^{m}$, the second term being the Tate-twist eigenspace on the coinvariants. It feeds the bound [`groupCohomology.finrank_inflationImage_le_finrank_invariants_add_finrank_invariants_dualTwist`](thm.html#groupCohomology.finrank_inflationImage_le_finrank_invariants_add_finrank_invariants_dualTwist), part of the Galois-cohomology input to the numerical criterion; the proof proceeds through the computation of $\dim H^1$ for a cyclic group in terms of the invariants and the norm map.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_groupCohomology_finrank_H1_le_finrank_invariants_add_finrank_ker_of_cyclic_quotient.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_TateTwist

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
